__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env

# Saved SIAN result pages — ~49 MB of binary, and the parsed catalog below
# carries everything we need from them. Keep locally, out of git history.
indices/

# Downloaded scans and derivatives
data/*
scans/

# ...but the parsed catalog is the corpus manifest and is versioned, since the
# index PDFs it derives from are not in git and were saved by hand. It names
# ships, notations and URLs — no passenger, which is the line.
!data/catalog.jsonl

# Nothing under data/ is ever un-ignored again, and this is the reason:
# `data/truth/*.json` was versioned and pushed, and it holds names read by hand
# off passenger lists — real people, some of them children on those sheets and
# possibly alive. That is personal data and it does not belong in a public
# history. docs/DATA.md says how to rebuild every file under data/ instead.

# generated prototype assets (embeds an archive page)
prototype/build/

# model venv
.venv-ocr/
.venv-htr/
.venv/

# transcription cache (per-machine work product, not source)
data/transcriptions/
data/pagecache/
data/spike_*.json

# ...and hand-read ground truth is NOT versioned, whatever it costs the tests.
# It was, for a while, directly under the comment above forbidding it: six
# files, 156 passenger names off Brazilian arrival lists of the 1920s, pushed
# to a public remote. Allan settled it on 2026-09-07 — the truth set stays on
# the machine that made it. A fixture that has to live in git is a document old
# enough that nobody on it can be harmed by it; see data/fixtures below.

# The single exception, and the reason it is allowed is in its own file: one
# page of a Philadelphia arrival manifest of 1800. A work of the United States
# federal government, so uncopyrighted, and 226 years old, so nobody named on
# it can be harmed by it. It carries ruled columns, repetition marks in three
# notations and a braced family sharing a surname — nearly everything the code
# is written against — so the tests need not reach into a corpus that lives on
# one machine. See data/fixtures/PROVENANCE.md.
!data/fixtures/
!data/fixtures/*.md
!data/fixtures/*.json
!data/fixtures/*.jpg

# Nothing else under data/ is versioned, including the lists written by hand.
# Names belong to people in public records and this remote is public: a list of
# names in git is a list of names online, and a test that needs one skips
# instead. See tests/test_vocab.py.
